Sidekick Codex plugin

Install:
  Assemble a new plugin from bundled skills and current Archify and PPT Master resources; preserve the plugin files of an existing installation.
  Prepare and verify tool environments, register the Wsley marketplace, enable Sidekick and apply managed Codex settings.

Upgrade:
  Synchronize bundled skills, upstream tool resources and dependencies; verify environments before replacing changed plugin files and caches. Skip when Sidekick is not installed.
  Refresh marketplace registration, enable Sidekick and apply managed Codex settings.

Status:
  Report plugin registration, source records, Codex settings and tool environment status through bounded local queries.
  Check runtime packages, Chromium binding, presentation dependencies and system packages without launching a browser or contacting external services.

Requirements:
  Ubuntu, APT, AWK and a regular user with sudo access.
  An installed Codex CLI with plugin marketplace commands and marketplace-filtered listings through --marketplace.
  Installation and upgrades require access to the relevant GitHub, npm, Python, Chromium and APT sources.
  uv must support dependency plans through uv pip install --dry-run --output-format json; missing Node.js, pnpm and uv are prepared by the module.

Configuration:
  Marketplace root: ${XDG_DATA_HOME:-$HOME/.local/share}/sidekick
  Plugin source: ${XDG_DATA_HOME:-$HOME/.local/share}/sidekick/plugin
  Plugin registration: sidekick@wsley; installed plugin files are managed by the Codex plugin cache.
  Codex configuration: ${CODEX_HOME:-$HOME/.codex}/config.toml
  Managed environments: ${XDG_DATA_HOME:-$HOME/.local/share}/sidekick/runtimes

  Entry skill: sidekick:mira; describe project work naturally for task coordination and specialist selection.
  Install repairs environments and managed settings without refreshing existing skills; use wsley upgrade sidekick to synchronize skills and tool resources.
  Manage one <wsley-sidekick> block in developer_instructions, directing Mira to resume unfinished work after compaction or handoffs; preserve text outside the block.
  Set agents.max_concurrent_threads_per_session to 20 on install and upgrade; preserve other settings, custom roles and TOML comments.

  Bundled skills provide methods and automatic specialist selection under the target project's contracts; each skill carries its license and upstream references.
  Archify and PPT Master resources are acquired from the sources in assets/upstream.json and bundled under vendor/; skills-lock.json records acquired revisions rather than pinning future upgrades.
  runtime-packages.json records browser and MCP package versions; mcp.json points to managed executable paths.

  The module prepares the browser CLI, Chromium and draw.io MCP server; environment verification includes an offline browser launch.
  Archify uses runtimes/chromium through ARCHIFY_CHROME; ARCHIFY_UPDATE_CHECK_DISABLED=1 disables its independent update check.
  Presentations use Python 3.12, vendor/ppt-master/requirements.txt and the system tools in components.tsv; valid environments and matching runtime packages are reused.
  Project dependencies, accounts, credentials and remote services remain project or task configuration; browser and Python caches use their tools' storage settings.

  Skills organize necessary task materials under the project's .sidekick/ directory; build output, tool caches and ordinary command output retain their own ownership.
  Assembly or environment validation failure preserves active plugin files and Codex configuration. Activation failure restores affected plugin files and configuration; completed dependency changes remain.
  Global skill directories are not modified.
  Open a new Codex conversation after installation or upgrade to load the plugin and entry instruction.
